research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log-8022-research/audit/wave5-topology-function-spaces.provenance.jsonl-32-{"id": "ex-the-exponential-law-worked-on-the-line", "statement": "ai-altered", "proof": "ai-generated", "evidence": "semantic-source", "urls": ["https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/compact-open+topology", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compact-open_topology", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exponential_object"], "rationale": "A worked instance of the sourced exponential law on X = Z = Y = R, with the multiplication map as the chosen f. Multiplication on R x R is continuous, its transpose is the family of multiplication-by-z maps, each Lipschitz with constant |z|, and local compactness of R is Munkres Sec. 29 Example 1. Every ingredient is standard; the composition into one traced example, and the direct estimate |x||z-z_0| <= iota(m)|z-z_0| on [-m,m] replacing the tube lemma, are local. Hence ai-altered. Local verification.", "alpha_concurred": false, "at": "2026-08-05"}
research/audit/wave12-dispatch/audit-beta-a4r2.log:8023:research/audit/wave5-topology-function-spaces.provenance.jsonl:33:{"id": "ex-dini-on-the-unit-interval", "statement": "ai-altered", "proof": "ai-generated", "evidence": "semantic-source", "urls": ["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dini%27s_theorem", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uniform_limit_theorem"], "rationale": "A worked instance of the sourced Dini theorem on [0,1] together with its standard sharpness discussion. The clipped identities s_k(t) = min{t, 1 - a_k} form a nondecreasing sequence of continuous functions converging pointwise to the continuous identity, which is a routine instance rather than a novel construction, and the failure clause reuses this page's ramps to show that continuity of the limit cannot be dropped, which is the standard remark accompanying Dini's theorem. Specialisation of a sourced theorem plus a standard sharpness witness, hence ai-altered. Local verification; note that the positive half is also proved directly by the bound |s_k(t) - t| <= a_k, independent of Dini.", "alpha_concurred": false, "at": "2026-08-05"}
